    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d296-a4">

                <pb facs="0547" n="513" sameAs="frus:frus1870/pg513"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">No. 4.</seg></opener>
                <head>Mr. Elmore to Mr. A. P. Hovey.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1870-09-14"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >September,</hi> 14, — 7.15 a. m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear General</hi>: The minister says he is sorry
                    he can do nothing in the affair, and that the colonel need fear nothing, being
                    with you.</p>
                <p>I am not well of the throat; I can hardly speak.</p>
                <p>Yours sincerely,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>ELMORE.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>General A. P. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hovey,</hi>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
